# Writer 9 (beside MC-X-F12): pay's at reads pd, an input whose row governs 2027..: L §4.3 "The at ends every
# chain, so it reads nothing law-dated itself", L §8.3 `move <m>'s at reads law-dated <x>`. snap12:
# REFCORE-NOT-YET (the interpreter guard at the read).
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input age3: int
input amt: money PLN
input pay_day: date
input pd: date

move pay: transfers
  on pay_day
  at pd
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

ask q: bal(konto, 2027-12-31)

version v_act
  cite act
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  pd = 2027-03-01 "pd"

version v_f
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  age3 = 3 "the age"
  pay_day = 2027-02-01
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2027-01-01 start

version v_amt
  cite act
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "amt"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE move pay's at reads law-dated pd (m.tally:17)
